  "notes": "Los Angeles pop/dance production-and-songwriting collective. The one genuinely specific drum claim in the entry is a structural habit rather than a groove — \"a documented habit of a fill or stutter at the end of every fourth bar\" — so `fills.smallEveryBars` is 4 with `fillBeforeSection` true and the roll positions land on `bar_4`, which is the parameter this model exists to carry. The rest follows: \"clipped programmed kick and layered clap on 2&4, 16th hats … percussion is bright and dry\", which is a hard-transient short-tail snare with a doubled clap at a tight offset, `hihat.base` 16th at a high fill density, and a hard-quantised humanize block. The 808 is authored because the entry names it — \"filtered pumping synth sub on 8ths for the dance records; 808 sub with short slides for the R&B-facing ones\" — as `counter_riff`, with the pumping sub remaining the bassline on `offbeat_8ths`. Harmony is \"minor-mode 4-bar loops with a relative-major pre-chorus lift\" over which \"their radio-facing records favour a narrow-range topline over an unchanging vamp\", so a major family sits beside the minor ones, `harmonicRhythm` leans vamp, and the melody register spans barely an octave — the narrowest authored on the producer side of this section. \"Records combine a stacked choir-style vocal bed with a plucked or bell instrumental hook\" is the two-style counter, and \"the instrumental post-chorus is the standard hook slot\" is the arrangement. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a medium-high rating because the research says the parametric detail is \"partly lane-derived\", and its own [LOW-CONF] mark on the narrow-topline claim is repeated here; every drum probability, the humanize pair and `bpm.mode` 112 (the midpoint of the stated 100—125 band) are INFERRED.",
